# ===========================================================================
#  Credentials for `npm run sandbox:pass --workspace=apps/server`, and
#  NOTHING ELSE.
# ===========================================================================
#
#  Copy this file to `apps/server/.env.sandbox` (gitignored) and fill in the
#  three values under REQUIRED. That is the whole list.
#
#  The sandbox pass calls Randox's `stes-` sandbox and writes the responses to
#  src/modules/randox/specs/sandbox-responses/. It has no database, issues no
#  sessions and signs no files, so it does NOT want DATABASE_URL, the JWT
#  secrets, CSRF_SECRET, ENCRYPTION_KEY, FILE_SIGNING_SECRET, APP_BASE_URL or
#  API_BASE_URL. Those belong in `.env`, which is the SERVER's configuration.
#
#  Anything already set in the real environment wins over this file, and this
#  file wins over `.env`.
#
#  These are secrets. `.env.sandbox` is gitignored; keep it that way.

# --- REQUIRED -------------------------------------------------------------

# From the NEXUS developer portal. Sent as Ocp-Apim-Subscription-Key.
RANDOX_NEXUS_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=

# The Azure B2C ROPC service account, created in the developer portal rather
# than issued by Randox — both auth documents say "the username created within
# the Developer Portal". One pair covers both APIs unless you were given two.
RANDOX_USERNAME=
RANDOX_PASSWORD=

# --- OPTIONAL: the Clinic Booking half ------------------------------------
#
# A SEPARATE key from a SEPARATE developer portal. Leave it blank and the pass
# runs the Nexus flow alone and records in ANSWERS.md that questions 4 to 7
# went unasked and why — it does not fail. Booking is not in this portal's
# scope (see the VITE_BOOKING_ENABLED note in CLAUDE.md), so blank is the
# ordinary case rather than an incomplete setup.
RANDOX_BOOKING_SUBSCRIPTION_KEY=

# Only if Randox issued you a different service account per API.
# RANDOX_NEXUS_USERNAME=
# RANDOX_NEXUS_PASSWORD=
# RANDOX_BOOKING_USERNAME=
# RANDOX_BOOKING_PASSWORD=

# --- OPTIONAL: overrides you will almost certainly not need ---------------
#
# Every documented, non-secret value is already defaulted in
# src/modules/randox/documentedDefaults.ts — both `stes-` base URLs, both B2C
# client ids, both scopes, the shared token endpoint, the two booking service
# ids (787 UK / 788 ROI) and the sandbox test location. The pass REFUSES to
# run against a base URL that is not a `stes-` host, and refuses outright
# under NODE_ENV=production.

# LocationId 30, "Clinic Location Crumlin", which Randox confirm has real
# availability. The collection's own examples use 15, which may have an empty
# diary — and an empty diary and a broken integration look identical.
# SANDBOX_LOCATION_ID=30

# How long to keep polling GetOrderStatus. Defaults to 20 minutes when the
# booking half runs, and 2 when it does not: an unbooked pending order does
# not progress, so one status call is all question 1 needs.
# SANDBOX_STATUS_TIMEOUT_MINUTES=

# Set only if GetMyClinicDetails cannot tell the pass which clinic it is.
# RANDOX_CLINIC_ID=
# RANDOX_TEST_CLINIC_LOCATION_ID=

# UK (787) or ROI (788). Only affects the booking half.
# RANDOX_BOOKING_REGION=UK

# A DIAGNOSTIC LEVER, not a setting. Both credentials are documented as
# required together; turn the bearer off only to bisect an unexplained 401.
# RANDOX_BEARER_TOKEN_ENABLED=true
